{"step_index":384,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:11:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T03:41:05+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T03:41:10+05:30\nThe search for \"\"auto_map\" huggingface custom model_type AutoConfig AutoModelForCausalLM\" returned the following summary:\nTo use a custom model architecture with Hugging Face's `Auto` classes (such as `AutoConfig` and `AutoModelForCausalLM`), you must implement an `auto_map` in your `config.json` file. This mapping tells the Transformers library which Python modules and classes to load when `from_pretrained` is called[1][2][3].\n\n### 1. Structure Your Custom Files\nEnsure your model repository includes the necessary Python files for your configuration and model architecture[1][4].\n*   **`configuration_*.py`**: Contains your custom configuration class (e.g., `MyCustomConfig`), which must subclass `PreTrainedConfig` and define a unique `model_type`[5][4].\n*   **`modeling_*.py`**: Contains your custom model class (e.g., `MyCustomModelForCausalLM`), which must reference your custom config class[5][4].\n\n### 2. Configure `config.json`\nYour `config.json` file must include the `auto_map` field[6][2]. This dictionary maps the standard Hugging Face Auto classes to your specific files and class names[7][1].\n\n```json\n{\n  \"model_type\": \"my-custom-model\",\n  \"architectures\": [\"MyCustomModelForCausalLM\"],\n  \"auto_map\": {\n    \"AutoConfig\": \"configuration_file_name.MyCustomConfig\",\n    \"AutoModel\": \"modeling_file_name.MyCustomModel\",\n    \"AutoModelForCausalLM\": \"modeling_file_name.MyCustomModelForCausalLM\"\n  }\n}\n```\n*   **`AutoConfig`**: Points to your custom configuration class[1][2].\n*   **`AutoModelForCausalLM`**: Points to the class in your modeling file that implements the causal language modeling task[8][9].\n\n### 3. Loading the Model\nBecause your model uses custom, non-standard code, you must explicitly enable the `trust_remote_code=True` flag when loading it[10][2][11].\n\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM, AutoConfig\n\n# The library will now look at your auto_map in config.json \n# and import the classes from your .py files.\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n    \"path/to/your/model\", \n    trust_remote_code=True\n)\n```\n\n### Important Tips\n*   **`trust_remote_code=True`**: This is required because the library is executing arbitrary Python code from your repository[10][11]. Only load models from sources you trust.\n*   **Registration**: While you can manually register classes using `AutoConfig.register()` and `AutoModel.register()` in a local script, using the `auto_map` in `config.json` is the standard way to ensure your model works automatically for others when shared on the Hugging Face Hub[12][13].\n*   **File Naming**: Ensure the filenames (e.g., `modeling_file_name.py`) are correct and accessible in the root of your model directory or the path provided[1][2].\n\nSources:\n[1] [gilesthomas.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCMXJ6LvUZ6IKQeFit0Mcz9D_de0LpaCk1D0sZY5M34SO3UYTUs5NXFXrjJ3Q7vwOe1pX0tsY0d7rDyDIAgKrVPuFlcvJfYZdX94OsX5_2NXaPq-leMxEsj0jIb-r8dfVz2m1lZO6k-ZiKC-kYTGooFVWhM-idEQK4VI_GC049w9PbhhwF9Xiix4TPVe_b_SeeSrPSAF_bfcLLWg==)\n[2] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHJoLAoV4Xa1ztkJInJzUtxHrXiieHGPOVLnQA59HdLTww5M14WQ5sH896oarjxcmwh5cq4omzEDXf_SDy9Vg2s3cmRrUv924JtSIHVAtYHJQWIisSg2jn0AHFjX97Ak3nPrAMW3VjguBE8Cy2R28ZXoho3sVU2RLw=)\n[3] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH7Be3PJZ64coahSEoix9sA7jDORu3jdSXNXGIIGYVMx55PXOYxIQfT2pYVeTY1y9S1UV1kUFEMDghn5m28y_BmtXzgH7vSPGkItYtFh-r7JRb1kqZ9Fml2AxAfMuuFgJYLOvL77Kiy2LLu-ZveDEHIol5XVY8R9ga3AhbCtbER3jxg8VQxFNB51Z-jJFkgLkXz2A==)\n[4] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH-kqy2Wz4uy4Ydirqi9U4P0OP-RZnQY5CoSwIEIQO07CSNtzpqQ1nISr6ZuM